> Is it safe to assume that the inclusion of predictors (all time-invariant) is the reason for the discrepancy?

Yes, the parameter estimates are covariances between residuals, so standardized estimates are partial correlations, not the zero-order (model-implied) correlations you get from lavInspect(fit. "cor.lv <http://cor.lv>").  In an unconditional model, they are the same because the residual variance == the total variance.

